#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise {#learn-the-noise}"
msgstr "Matutuhan ang noise {#learn-the-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we run the experiments, we learn the noise model affecting the "
"entangling gates and measurements in the circuit. Having an accurate noise "
"model is necessary to effectively mitigate error. Learning the noise just "
"before executing the experiments gives the best chance of the noise model "
"faithfully describing the actual noise affecting the gates during "
"execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago natin patakbuhin ang mga eksperimento, matututuhan natin ang noise "
"model na nakakaapekto sa entangling gates at measurements sa circuit. Ang "
"pagkakaroon ng tumpak na noise model ay kinakailangan upang epektibong ma-"
"mitigate ang error. Ang pag-aaral ng noise bago mismo isagawa ang mga "
"eksperimento ay nagbibigay ng pinakamahusay na pagkakataon na ang noise "
"model ay tapat na maglarawan ng aktwal na noise na nakakaapekto sa gates "
"habang isinasagawa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we learn the noise, we need to find the unique 2-qubit layers in our "
"circuit, so we can minimize the number of shots needed to learn the noise "
"for the entire circuit. We use ``find_unique_box_instructions`` from "
"``samplomatic`` to provide us the unique layers from the boxed circuit, "
"including the measurement layer. These are the layers we pass to the noise "
"learner.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago natin matutuhan ang noise, kailangan nating hanapin ang mga unique "
"2-qubit layer sa ating circuit, upang ma-minimize natin ang bilang ng shots "
"na kailangan upang matutuhan ang noise para sa buong circuit. Ginagamit "
"natin ang ``find_unique_box_instructions`` mula sa ``samplomatic`` upang "
"ibigay sa atin ang mga unique layer mula sa boxed circuit, kasama na ang "
"measurement layer. Ito ang mga layer na ipinapasa natin sa noise learner.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once we know the layers, we can learn the noise. There are a few parameters "
"we consider:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag alam na natin ang mga layer, maaari na nating matutuhan ang noise. May"
" ilang parameter na isinasaalang-alang natin:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`num_randomizations`: The number of random circuits to use per learning "
"circuit configuration\n"
msgstr ""
"`num_randomizations`: Ang bilang ng random circuits na gagamitin sa bawat "
"learning circuit configuration\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`shots_per_randomization`: Total number of shots to use per random learning "
"circuit\n"
msgstr ""
"`shots_per_randomization`: Kabuuang bilang ng shots na gagamitin sa bawat "
"random learning circuit\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`layer_pair_depths`: The circuit depths (measured in number of pairs) to use"
" in learning experiments.\n"
msgstr ""
"`layer_pair_depths`: Ang circuit depths (sinusukat sa bilang ng pairs) na "
"gagamitin sa learning experiments.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`post_selection`: We will use edge-based post-selection during learning "
"using `rx` gates to implement the post-measurement pulses\n"
msgstr ""
"`post_selection`: Gagamit tayo ng edge-based post-selection habang nag-aaral"
" gamit ang `rx` gates upang i-implementa ang post-measurement pulses\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-"
"observable/output_5.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-"
"observable/output_5.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Associate circuit boxes with learned noise {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-"
"learned-noise}"
msgstr ""
"Iugnay ang circuit boxes sa learned noise {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-"
"learned-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we create a mapping between the ``InjectNoise`` reference IDs of each "
"box to the learned noise model (`PauliLindbladMap`) affecting the entangling"
" gates in that box.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, gumagawa tayo ng mapping sa pagitan ng ``InjectNoise`` reference IDs "
"ng bawat box patungo sa learned noise model (`PauliLindbladMap`) na "
"nakakaapekto sa entangling gates sa box na iyon.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Propagate the observable through the learned anti-noise to get a noise-"
"mitigating observable {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-"
"noise-to-get-a-noise-mitigating-observable}"
msgstr ""
"Ipropagate ang observable sa learned anti-noise upang makakuha ng noise-"
"mitigating observable {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-"
"noise-to-get-a-noise-mitigating-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As discussed above, this is done in two steps. First, we propagate an anti-"
"noise generator to the end of the circuit. After that, we propagate the "
"observable through that evolved generator. This process is repeated for each"
" anti-noise generator in the circuit. In this implementation, each generator"
" in a given layer is propagated to the end of the circuit in parallel. "
"Additionally, Python multiprocessing is used to perform both the forward-"
"propagation of the anti-noise as well as the back-propagation of the "
"observable in parallel. This prevents a pile-up of evolved generators in "
"memory and also maximizes compute resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng tinalakay sa itaas, ito ay ginagawa sa dalawang hakbang. Una, "
"ipropagate natin ang isang anti-noise generator hanggang sa katapusan ng "
"circuit. Pagkatapos noon, ipropagate natin ang observable sa pamamagitan ng "
"evolved generator na iyon. Ang prosesong ito ay inuulit para sa bawat anti-"
"noise generator sa circuit. Sa implementation na ito, ang bawat generator sa"
" isang ibinigay na layer ay ipinopropagate sa katapusan ng circuit nang "
"parallel. Bukod pa rito, ang Python multiprocessing ay ginagamit upang "
"isagawa ang parehong forward-propagation ng anti-noise pati na rin ang back-"
"propagation ng observable nang parallel. Pinipigilan nito ang pile-up ng "
"evolved generators sa memorya at kasabay nito ay napapakinabangan ang "
"compute resources.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When running PNA, you will always need to provided a noisy circuit and "
"observable. If your noisy circuit is a boxed circuit with `InjectNoise` "
"annotations, you will need to provide the mapping we created in the step "
"above. One can also pass a non-boxed circuit containing "
"``PauliLindbladError`` instructions from ``qiskit-aer``. In that case, "
"``refs_to_noise_models`` does not need to be provided. In addition to the "
"primary inputs, users will want to consider:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nagpapatakbo ng PNA, kakailanganin mong palaging magbigay ng noisy "
"circuit at observable. Kung ang iyong noisy circuit ay isang boxed circuit "
"na may `InjectNoise` annotations, kailangan mong ibigay ang mapping na "
"ginawa natin sa hakbang sa itaas. Maaari ka ring magpasa ng non-boxed "
"circuit na naglalaman ng ``PauliLindbladError`` instructions mula sa "
"``qiskit-aer``. Sa kasong iyon, hindi na kailangang ibigay ang "
"``refs_to_noise_models``. Bukod sa primary inputs, gugustuhin ng mga user na"
" isaalang-alang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`max_err_terms`: The number of terms to keep in each anti-noise generator as"
" it is forward-propagated. Allowing this to be larger generally increases "
"accuracy, but this behavior is not guaranteed to be monotonic.\n"
msgstr ""
"`max_err_terms`: Ang bilang ng mga terminong panatilihin sa bawat anti-noise"
" generator habang ito ay forward-propagated. Ang pagpapahintulot na lumaki "
"ito ay sa pangkalahatan ay nagpapataas ng katumpakan, ngunit ang pag-"
"uugaling ito ay hindi garantisado na maging monotonic.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`max_obs_terms`: The number of terms to keep in the noise-mitigating "
"observable, $\\tilde{O}$, as it is back-propagated through the evolved anti-"
"noise. Larger values generally increase accuracy, but it is not guaranteed "
"to do so monotonically.\n"
msgstr ""
"`max_obs_terms`: Ang bilang ng mga terminong panatilihin sa noise-mitigating"
" observable, $\\tilde{O}$, habang ito ay back-propagated sa pamamagitan ng "
"evolved anti-noise. Ang mas malalaking values ay sa pangkalahatan ay "
"nagpapataas ng katumpakan, ngunit hindi garantisado na gagawin ito nang "
"monotonic.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`num_processes`: The number of cores to dedicate to the process. Remember, "
"the generators are forward-propagated and applied to the observable in "
"parallel.\n"
msgstr ""
"`num_processes`: Ang bilang ng cores na ilalaan sa proseso. Tandaan, ang "
"generators ay forward-propagated at inilalapat sa observable nang "
"parallel.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`search_step`: The back-propagation step uses a greedy method to "
"approximately conjugate two operators in the Pauli basis. This method can be"
" sped up by increasing ``search_step``. See the [pauli-prop "
"docs](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) for more info.\n"
msgstr ""
"`search_step`: Ang back-propagation step ay gumagamit ng greedy method upang"
" humigit-kumulang i-conjugate ang dalawang operator sa Pauli basis. Ang "
"method na ito ay maaaring mapabilis sa pamamagitan ng pagpapataas ng "
"``search_step``. Tingnan ang [pauli-prop "
"docs](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) para sa karagdagang info.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`num_to_measure`: While this variable isn't an input to "
"``generate_noise_mitigating_observable``, we use it to control how many "
"terms from $\\tilde{O}$ we actually want to measure. Here we will only "
"measure the top 30 terms, which are the original terms in our observable. "
"The terms have now been re-scaled such that measuring them has the effect of"
" mitigating the learned gate noise. Although we only measure 30 terms from "
"$\\tilde{O}$, it is often still useful to allow it to grow large, as that "
"increases the precision of the leading terms' scaling factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"`num_to_measure`: Bagaman ang variable na ito ay hindi input sa "
"``generate_noise_mitigating_observable``, ginagamit natin ito upang "
"kontrolin kung ilang termino mula sa $\\tilde{O}$ ang gusto nating talagang "
"sukatin. Dito, susukatin lamang natin ang nangungunang 30 na termino, na "
"siyang orihinal na mga termino sa ating observable. Ang mga termino ay na-"
"rescale na ngayon nang sa gayon ang pagsukat sa mga ito ay may epekto ng "
"pag-mitigate sa learned gate noise. Bagaman 30 termino lamang ang ating "
"sinusukat mula sa $\\tilde{O}$, madalas ay kapaki-pakinabang pa rin na "
"payagan itong lumaki, dahil pinapataas niyon ang katumpakan ng scaling "
"factors ng nangungunang mga termino.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-"
"observable/output_6.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-"
"observable/output_6.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transform the measurement bases to canonical form {#transform-the-"
"measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"
msgstr ""
"I-transform ang measurement bases sa canonical form {#transform-the-"
"measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we will find a minimal set of bases to measure such that we can fully "
"cover every Pauli term in the measured observable (***many observables may "
"be measured simultaneously if they commute qubit-wise***). Since we are only"
" measuring the terms in our original observable, which is the sum of all "
"single-`Z` Paulis, a single basis is needed -- the all-`Z` basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, hahanapin natin ang isang minimal na set ng bases na susukatin "
"upang ganap nating masaklaw ang bawat Pauli term sa measured observable "
"(***maraming observables ang maaaring sukatin nang sabay-sabay kung qubit-"
"wise silang nag-c-commute***). Dahil sinusukat lamang natin ang mga termino "
"sa ating orihinal na observable, na siyang sum ng lahat ng single-`Z` "
"Paulis, isang basis lamang ang kailangan -- ang all-`Z` basis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to finding a set of Pauli measurement bases, we need to map "
"these Pauli terms to the canonical form expected by the ``Executor`` "
"primitive. For more information on canonical qubit ordering, visit the "
"[samplomatic "
"docs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-"
"ordering-convention).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod sa paghahanap ng set ng Pauli measurement bases, kailangan nating "
"i-map ang Pauli terms na ito sa canonical form na inaasahan ng ``Executor`` "
"primitive. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon sa canonical qubit ordering, "
"bisitahin ang [samplomatic "
"docs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-"
"ordering-convention).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specify how to sample in the ``QuantumProgram`` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-"
"the-quantumprogram}"
msgstr ""
"Tukuyin kung paano mag-sample sa ``QuantumProgram`` {#specify-how-to-sample-"
"in-the-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ``QuantumProgram`` is where we specify how to sample the experiment:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ``QuantumProgram`` ay kung saan natin tinutukoy kung paano i-sample ang "
"eksperimento:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``template_circuit``: The circuit containing all the gates necessary to "
"implement all desired randomizations (from twirling randomizations, "
"parameters, etc).\n"
msgstr ""
"``template_circuit``: Ang circuit na naglalaman ng lahat ng gates na "
"kailangan upang i-implementa ang lahat ng nais na randomizations (mula sa "
"twirling randomizations, parameters, atbp).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``samplex``: An object definining a probability distribution over all "
"possible circuit randomizations from which to sample.\n"
msgstr ""
"``samplex``: Isang object na tumutukoy sa probability distribution sa lahat "
"ng posibleng circuit randomizations kung saan magsa-sample.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "``samplex_arguments``: Bindings necessary to fully define the samplex\n"
msgstr ""
"``samplex_arguments``: Mga binding na kinakailangan upang ganap na tukuyin "
"ang samplex\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``basis_changes``: Here is where we specify a set of bases to measure which "
"will cover all of the Pauli terms in the measured observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"``basis_changes``: Dito tinutukoy natin ang isang set ng bases na susukatin "
"na sasaklaw sa lahat ng Pauli terms sa measured observable.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``noise_scales.ref``: We set each noise layer's scale to `0.0` to prevent "
"any additional noise from being injected into our samples\n"
msgstr ""
"``noise_scales.ref``: Itinakda natin ang scale ng bawat noise layer sa `0.0`"
" upang maiwasan ang anumang karagdagang noise na ma-inject sa ating "
"samples\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``pauli_lindblad_maps``: Required if ``noise_scales`` are passed. This just "
"maps noise layers to the associated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"``pauli_lindblad_maps``: Kinakailangan kung ipinapasa ang ``noise_scales``. "
"Ito ay nagma-map lamang ng noise layers sa kaukulang noise model.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``shape``: A shape tuple to extend the implicit shape defined by "
"``samplex_arguments``. Non-trivial axes introduced by this extension "
"enumerate randomizations.\n"
msgstr ""
"``shape``: Isang shape tuple para palawakin ang implicit shape na tinutukoy "
"ng ``samplex_arguments``. Ang non-trivial axes na ipinakilala ng "
"pagpapalawig na ito ay nag-e-enumerate ng randomizations.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample the circuit using the ``Executor`` primitive prototype {#sample-the-"
"circuit-using-the-executor-primitive-prototype}"
msgstr ""
"I-sample ang circuit gamit ang ``Executor`` primitive prototype {#sample-"
"the-circuit-using-the-executor-primitive-prototype}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we have defined our ``QuantumProgram``, executing the experiment is"
" straightforward. We simply instantiate the ``Executor`` object, provide it "
"the backend, and run the program.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayong natukoy na natin ang ating ``QuantumProgram``, ang pag-execute ng "
"eksperimento ay simple. Itinatatag natin ang ``Executor`` object, ibinibigay"
" sa ito ang backend, at pinapatakbo ang program.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Post-process the samples to calculate an error-mitigated expectation value "
"{#post-process-the-samples-to-calculate-an-error-mitigated-expectation-"
"value}"
msgstr ""
"I-post-process ang samples upang makalkula ang error-mitigated expectation "
"value {#post-process-the-samples-to-calculate-an-error-mitigated-"
"expectation-value}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To calculate an error-mitigated expectation value, we will:\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang makalkula ang error-mitigated expectation value, gagawin natin ang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the TREX scaling factors based on the learned noise affecting the "
"measurements\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin ang TREX scaling factors batay sa learned noise na nakakaapekto "
"sa measurements\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate a mask for keeping only post-selected samples\n"
msgstr "Bumuo ng mask para panatilihin lamang ang post-selected samples\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the ``executor_expectation_values`` function from ``qiskit-addon-utils``"
" for combining all of the data into an error-mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang ``executor_expectation_values`` function mula sa ``qiskit-addon-"
"utils`` para pagsamahin ang lahat ng data sa isang error-mitigated "
"expectation value.\n"

